  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USAID&#x2019;s End Malaria Project (Malaria Insecticide Treated Net (ITN) Distribution)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Democratic Republic of the Congo):  Malaria remains the single greatest cause of illness and death in the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC), killing around 22,800 Congolese in 2021. Preventive malaria interventions are an important, cost-effective step in tackling DRC&apos;s high malaria burden, and insecticide-treated nets (ITNs) are a highly effective means of preventing infection and reducing malaria transmission. USAID&apos;s End Malaria Activity will use FY 2022 funds to distribute ITNs through mass campaigns and school-based distribution in targeted provinces. It will also strengthen the capacity of the National Malaria Control Program to plan and execute ITN distribution. All mass distribution campaigns will use a door-to-door strategy instead of large awareness-raising events to minimize the spread of COVID-19 by avoiding mass gatherings. In addition, all actors involved in distribution will wear face masks, use hand sanitizer, and observe social distancing...This activity will contribute to Mission Objective 4.1 (Strengthen institutional and community capacity to prevent outbreaks from becoming pandemics as well as respond to and overcome frequent public health and humanitarian emergencies) by supporting the DRC&apos;s goal to accelerate a reduction in maternal and child deaths. Healthy women and children contribute to more productive, self-reliant, and stable communities, thereby maximizing American taxpayer investments and reducing threats to U.S. national security.....</narrative>
  </description>
